Unicode confusables data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

pipeline/confusables.py is generated from the Unicode Consortium's UTS #39
data file confusables.txt (Unicode 18.0.0, dated 2026-08-06), vendored at
scripts/data/unicode/confusables.txt with its copyright header intact:

    Copyright (c) 2026 Unicode, Inc.
    Unicode and the Unicode Logo are registered trademarks of Unicode, Inc.
    in the U.S. and other countries.

    Source: https://www.unicode.org/Public/security/latest/confusables.txt
    Licence: Unicode License v3, https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

The vendored data file is a build input only and is not shipped in the image;
the generated module carries derived mapping tables (see its header).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party corpus samples
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The injection test corpus under tests/corpus/attacks/ carries capped,
seed-fixed samples from three MIT-licensed datasets. The benign counter-corpus
under tests/corpus/benign/ carries a fourth MIT-licensed dataset, NotInject,
excerpts of CC-BY-4.0 arXiv papers (the next section after the MIT text), and
excerpts of Wikinews, the Python documentation, the Rust book and project
READMEs / changelogs (the last section).
Every sampled payload was re-rendered (as a search snippet, a page body or a
text upload, with every host rewritten to an RFC 2606 reserved name) by
scripts/corpus/ingest/. These records are test data only; none is shipped
in the image. Each record's `source` object names its dataset, licence,
revision and upstream row.

